<details><summary>How to install or upgrade</summary><ol>
<li>Close the game and MO2. Back up your complete <strong>bin</strong> and <strong>db</strong> folders, original OptiScaler proxy and <strong>OptiScaler.ini</strong>. Extract this runtime ZIP’s bin and db folders together into Anomaly, preserving their paths. This is an engine replacement, not an MO2 mod.</li>
<li>Keep only one OptiScaler proxy. Use the supplied patched <strong>dxgi.dll</strong> and INI; do not load an older proxy under another name. When upgrading, back up and move the obsolete <strong>nvngx.dll_dlssnr.dll</strong> helper out of bin. <strong>Keep nvngx_dlssnr.dll</strong> — that is the separate NR model.</li>
<li>For GAMMA, install Bodycam GAMMA Patch 1.1.0. Keep the matching DLSS shader compatibility patch below Bodycam, SSS and Atmospherics; it requires SSS 23.5. Select your installed Atmospherics version and Wearable Devices only when present. Disable older conflicting DLSS/FSR patches.</li>
<li>Loose MO2 files override db archives. Use the matching FG UI/scope patch below the older UI and shader patches. In particular, <strong>modxml_dlss_options.script</strong>, <strong>st_monolith_dlss.xml</strong> and <strong>scope_reference_image.ps</strong> must match this engine. Older loose files can hide the new controls or show obsolete launcher instructions.</li>
<li>Clear the shader cache, keep MSAA off and reload the level after installing the shaders. Launch normally through <strong>MO2 → Play</strong>. No special launcher or environment variable is needed.</li>
<li>In <strong>Video → Basic</strong>, select DLSS/DLAA and quality, then Apply. Set <strong>NVIDIA frame generation → On (2x)</strong> and Apply. PiP frame generation is separate for supported Bodycam Reference scopes. Unsupported scopes, night vision, thermal views, menus and loading can suspend FG. Press <strong>Insert</strong> for OptiScaler. Keep <strong>FrameGen.External=true</strong>, OptiScaler’s own FG off and <strong>OverlayMenu=false</strong>; the engine owns FG.</li>
</ol><p class="hint">To roll back, restore your complete backed-up engine, proxy, INI and matching UI/shader setup. Remove only obsolete FG test archives identified by the release instructions, after backup. Do not delete unrelated db archives. Check the <a href={download.url}>release installation notes</a> for the exact package contents and upgrade steps.</p></details>
